  "subject": "📚 Axios Finish Line: Book club boom",
  "date": "Wed, 09 Sep 2026 21:29:26 -0400",
  "body_text": "96 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n 🌊 Plus: Jersey shore sunset | Wednesday, September 09, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n View in browser \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n Axios Finish Line \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n By Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei &middot; Sep 09, 2026 \r\n \r\n \r\n Welcome back! Smart Brevity™ count: 291 words … 1 min. Copy edited by Amy Stern. \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 1 big thing: There&#x27;s a book club for that \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n Illustration: Brendan Lynch/Axios\n\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Americans may be reading less , but bookstores are thriving and book clubs are bringing people together.\n\n Book club events on Eventbrite jumped 33% during the first half of this year compared with the same time last year, Axios' Sami Sparber reports. 👀 The intrigue: The book club boom has been largely driven by \"hyper niche\" meetups that bring together readers who love the same genres or have the same hobbies, Eventbrite says.\n\n Readers are lacing up corsets and attaching prosthetic fairy ears to gather with fellow fans of the red-hot \" romantasy \" genre. They're reading together silently , sometimes not even the same book. Indie bookstores are hosting clubs for people who want to craft while they discuss books. 👻 Case in point: At Atlanta bookstore Offbeat Books , each book club has its own vibe, owner Lindsi Bollinger tells Axios.\n\n The horror club spills into movie talk, while the nonfiction club is run \"pretty much like a classroom,\" with PowerPoints, a projector and discussion questions. There's also a \" weird girl \" reading group — part of a literary trend celebrating books with messy, strange, complicated female protagonists. 👥 Between the lines: Book clubs are also getting a lift as younger people get more into offline hobbies and in-person hangouts.\n\n \"One of my favorite parts of book club is when we have ended the book club and people are just talking to each other … maybe making plans outside of the book club,\" says Hannah Mathews, a bookseller at Offbeat Books who facilitates the \"weird girl\" club. Share this story . \n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\nA MESSAGE FROM AXIOS\r\n\n \r\n Free Live Open House: See Smart Brevity in Action \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Communication breaks down when it's unclear. Join our free live Open House to see how Smart Brevity sharpens every update your team sends.\n\n Live demo of the Smart Brevity method Real before/after comms makeovers Q&A with an Axios HQ coach 👉 Save your spot .\n\n\r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n 2. Down the shore \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n Photo: Joan Fine A show-stopping late-summer sunset at Barnegat Lighthouse State Park in N.J., snapped by reader Joan Fine.\n\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; \r\n \r\n 🏁 Please invite your friends to join Finish Line . \n\n \r\n 👆 Like this comms style and format? It's called Smart Brevity®. Bring it to your org — via hands-on training or internal comms software — to harness its power and impact. \r\n &nbsp; Axios thanks our partners for supporting our journalism.\n Advertise with us. \n\n Read more about Axios' mission , ethics and how we use AI in our journalism . You can reach the authors by replying to this email.\nSponsorship has no influence on editorial content.\n\n Thank you for signing up for this Axios newsletter. To stop receiving this newsletter, unsubscribe or manage your email preferences . If someone forwarded this to you, sign up now to get Axios in your inbox.\n\n Axios, PO Box 101060, Arlington VA 22201 &nbsp; Follow Axios across:\n\n &nbsp; &nbsp; \r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;",
